   246	P_G(x_1,...,x_r;t)
   247	  = product_(a in A_G) (1-t*x^a)^(-1),               (3.3)
   248	```
   249	
   250	truncated to total `x`-weight eight.  The coefficient of `x^n t^g` is the
   251	number of unordered multisets of numerical germ signatures with total `n`
   252	and `g` germs.  Each canonical record contains this whole coefficient
   253	vector, its sum, and its least and greatest nonzero degrees.
   254	
   255	Three distinctions are essential.
   256	
   257	* The coordinate `n_i` is an intersection multiplicity, not a number of
   258	  germs.  For example, `u e_i+v e_j` can be one germ at one ADE node.
   259	* A germ is not automatically a distinct physical point.  Several germs
   260	  can share a smooth point, and all edge germs for the same edge begin at
   261	  its unique node.  Separating them can require further blowups.
   262	* The partitions in (3.3) are numerical germ-signature partitions.  They
   263	  do not count analytic moduli or locations, do not group germs into global
   264	  carrier curves, and are not quotiented by the stabilizer of the chosen
   265	  diagram representative.
   266	
   267	Every `n` has the unit-vertex partition consisting of `n_i` copies of
   268	`e_i`.  Consequently the maximum possible germ number is `w(n)`, with
   269	coefficient one.  A one-germ partition exists exactly when `n` itself has
   270	support on one vertex, or on both endpoints of one edge and nowhere else.
   271	The congruence (1.2) or (1.4) still applies to the total `n`; an individual
   272	branch need not separately be a Cartier divisor downstairs.
   273	
   274	## 4. The exact forest cut, and why it is conditional
   275	
   276	Let `T_E` denote the connected exceptional ADE tree in a fully resolved SNC
   277	boundary.  Any actual strict divisor supplies a collection of analytic
   278	branches, and their contact vectors give one of the partitions counted by
   279	(3.3).  Thus the computed minimum is a rigorous lower bound for the number
   280	of actual branches, although the converse realization of every counted
   281	partition is not claimed.  After the additional point blowups needed to
   282	separate tangencies or branches, distinct branches have distinct final
   283	attachment edges; several branches may have shared a physical crossing and
   284	an initial infinitely-near path before that separation.
   285	
   286	First suppose nothing is known about how the germs group into outside
   287	carriers.  For any enumerated `n`, its unit-vertex partition can be drawn as
   288	an abstract graph by assigning every atom a separate outside leaf.  The
   289	resulting graph is a tree: it is `T_E` with leaf paths attached.  This
   290	drawing does not construct simultaneous analytic branches or a Cartier
   291	equation; it proves only that the unlabelled numerical forest test contains
   292	no contradiction.  Hence neither a large coefficient, support on several
   293	Dynkin vertices, nor minimum germ
   294	count greater than one is by itself a forest contradiction.  This proves
   295	the exact negative result:
   296	
   297	```text
   298	local Cartan pair + cap + forest, without carrier data,
   299	rules out zero of the 16,360 cap-eight pairs.          (4.1)
   300	```
   301	
   302	Now add the genuinely stronger hypothesis that on one common embedded SNC
   303	resolution: (i) the inner graph consisting of `T_E` and any shared
   304	infinitely-near attachment trunks is connected; (ii) the reduced strict
   305	transforms of all relevant outside carriers form one connected subgraph
   306	disjoint from that inner graph before final attachments; and (iii) distinct
   307	analytic branches give distinct final joining edges.  Two such edges
   308	between these connected subgraphs make a cycle.  There can therefore be at
   309	most one analytic branch, so `n` must itself be an atom (3.1) or (3.2).
   310	
   311	This conditional cut is exact on the finite numerical list:
   312	
   313	| cap | raw all | raw one-germ | raw excluded | canonical all | canonical one-germ | canonical excluded |
   314	|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   315	| 8 | 16,360 | 718 | 15,642 | 12,238 | 563 | 11,675 |
   316	| 4, conditional | 772 | 198 | 574 | 646 | 163 | 483 |
   317	
   318	The table is not licensed merely because `R_str` is effective, because its
   319	support is connected downstairs, or because several numerical atoms begin
   320	at the same physical crossing.  One must establish the stated connected
   321	resolved outside subgraph and the separated final joining edges.  Nor
   322	does “one germ” mean “one Dynkin vertex”: an edge atom is one physical germ
